Ensure an ordinary bounded Task evidence entry exists via the existing workflow-evidence-ledger command; it is observation, not route authority.

Run .kent/scripts/workflow-release-cleanup from the actual Task H root with ONE closed JSON object: task_id={{.TaskId}}, incoming_transition=release_release_published, parameters containing exactly the fields below. Keep KENT_SESSION_ID inherited from your own Kent tool environment; never invent a caller ID or _kent Script envelope. The helper independently derives observable outcome; this route hint cannot bypass publication, resource or sealed-report proof.

Other idle historical Task Sessions on H are normal; never enumerate/select/leave them as cleanup owners.

On helper failure preserve resources and report the precise blocker; do not complete to Janitor. On success retain its exact flat output, close only your own background/tool processes, use the supported worktree leave for YOUR Session, and verify your current target is the primary workspace. Then use the normal Agent workflow completion to cleanup_task_janitor with the helper output fields unchanged. Do not call the seal helper again from primary. Stock Janitor/native Delete owns other idle Session retargeting and active/background admission; no bulk leave/delete, publication, fetch or new Session.

